+# Equipped header car pictures (2026-10-26)
+
+HCA01: Header and dropdown pictures show the saved, equipped livery and body-kit parts. HCA02: Reuse lightweight pictures instead of retaining a model in each menu widget. HCA03: Keep account, navigation and latest-selection guards. R01/Q01: Record native verification, original failures and a task-only review checkpoint.
+
+The user's current-livery/kit correction supersedes the standard-appearance restriction in `HEADER_CAR_LIGHTWEIGHT_2026_10_26.md`. The header and six alternative dropdown rows still display shared 176×112 textures. The active car remains excluded, clicking the car opens the dropdown, and clicking the name opens Profile. Existing slot bounds, stationary crossfade and dropdown motion remain.
+
+An App-owned cache captures an uncached equipped appearance through the existing simple-model profile studio, including saved livery colours/pattern/stickers and fitted parts. It uses one temporary cooperative studio, releases it after capture, and performs PNG decoding, alpha correction and encoding through one owned worker. Saved changes debounce for 0.35 seconds. Ordinary menu visits reuse the same texture; a new process can load the saved PNG without rebuilding a car. Default stock appearances use the bundled pictures without capturing anything.
+
+The cache key includes normalized appearance, car, records owner path, build, renderer and cache version. Customized textures and private PNG files are each bounded to 14 entries; PNG reads validate format, dimensions and a 128 KiB encoded-size limit. Account replacement cancels queued work and rejects stale completions. Live races, loading/background-work fences and account/restoring pages defer model captures. Unbought Garage previews do not alter the saved header appearance. A missing picture temporarily uses the bundled stock image until its current equipped capture is ready.
+
+Runtime changes are `game/ui/header_car_appearance_cache.gd`, `header_car_icons.gd`, `header_car_picker.gd`, three texture lookups in `profile_car.gd`, and App service binding/refresh hooks. The profile studio, car geometry, camera and materials remain unchanged. Concurrent appearance-sync API retirement and progressive Garage entry in App are preserved and excluded from the task patch.
+
+`test_header_equipped_cache.gd` runs the actual App with isolated local records and no service connection. It compares the cached image with an independently constructed equipped reference, verifies livery-only and kit-only refresh, rapid-edit debounce, disk reuse, corrupt-cache recovery, deferred work, account replacement, navigation and bounded resource ownership. The header/dropdown have zero Node3D nodes and zero SubViewports; the cache's measured peak is one temporary studio, with none retained when settled. `capture_profile_car.gd` keeps its existing input/save/name/motion checks and now expects the equipped cached picture.
+
+Actual commands use pinned Godot 4.7.2 through `scripts/dev.ps1`, with `APPDATA` and `LOCALAPPDATA` redirected to `build/header-car-appearance-appdata`:
+
+```powershell
+powershell -NoProfile -ExecutionPolicy Bypass -File scripts/dev.ps1 TestScript -ScriptPath res://tests/test_header_equipped_cache.gd -Graphical -RenderingMethod gl_compatibility
+powershell -NoProfile -ExecutionPolicy Bypass -File scripts/dev.ps1 TestScript -ScriptPath res://tests/test_header_equipped_cache.gd -Graphical -RenderingMethod mobile
+powershell -NoProfile -ExecutionPolicy Bypass -File scripts/dev.ps1 TestApp -CommandTimeoutSeconds 180
+powershell -NoProfile -ExecutionPolicy Bypass -File scripts/dev.ps1 TestScript -ScriptPath res://tests/test_menu_responsiveness.gd
+powershell -NoProfile -ExecutionPolicy Bypass -File scripts/dev.ps1 TestScript -ScriptPath res://tests/probe_header_equipped_baseline.gd -CommandTimeoutSeconds 180
+powershell -NoProfile -ExecutionPolicy Bypass -File scripts/dev.ps1 TestScript -ScriptPath res://tests/test_script_parse.gd
+```
+
+The interaction run additionally sets `BMT_PROFILE_CAR_OUTPUT=res://../docs/evidence/header-car-appearance-cache-2026-10-26/interaction` and `BMT_HEADER_MOTION_REVIEW=1`, then runs `TestScript -ScriptPath res://tests/capture_profile_car.gd -Graphical -RenderingMethod gl_compatibility -CommandTimeoutSeconds 180`. The current-App/no-cache control sets `BMT_HEADER_CACHE_CONTROL=1` before running the probe. The isolated pinned-engine UID helper in `build/header-car-texture-import/create_equipped_cache_uids.gd` creates only the three new script UIDs.
+
+Both native renderer suites pass 45 checks, including five cold/changed captures, a disk hit, maximum one studio and zero header worlds/viewports. Native interaction review retains all seven stock-car pictures, equipped caching, six visible alternatives, keyboard/mouse selection and saves, name navigation, long names and motion cleanup at three window sizes. Existing menu responsiveness passes 35 checks. Detailed final commands, diagnostics, retained intermediate results, hashes and patch verification are recorded in [the evidence report](evidence/header-car-appearance-cache-2026-10-26/report.json). Initial App shutdown closure leaks were corrected by binding the capture permission to a named App method and explicitly clearing cache-owned callbacks/jobs on exit. The current App suite passes all 141 assertions, but its runner exits 1 on a headless Dummy GeometryInstance PagedAllocator shutdown error. A control using current App with only this cache service disabled reproduces that same error; the task-start App control passes 141 assertions without it. Those controls change source only in isolated process memory and retain the concurrent sync API adapter. This separate shutdown diagnostic remains open; test assertions are unchanged.
+
+Review the [equipped header](evidence/header-car-appearance-cache-2026-10-26/gl_compatibility/equipped-header.png), [equipped dropdown](evidence/header-car-appearance-cache-2026-10-26/gl_compatibility/equipped-dropdown.png) and [kit-only update](evidence/header-car-appearance-cache-2026-10-26/gl_compatibility/changed-kit.png). Reload is required. Cold capture latency and phone frame/memory/thermal performance still require owner/device acceptance. No device attachment check or device test, APK, real authentication/purchase, owner-save/live mutation, deployment, staging, commit, merge or owner-process restart was performed.
